{"author":"did:key:z6Mkmz8SWiUshwDMszSqwzMngt7ScNmsEj7vZoFRLjpcZTm9","evaluation":{"digest":{"sha256":"4a483a342b7d8763f6fe7f868a5540cdb35b6dba5caffa61a646a08281f7be0d"}},"instructions":"Return exactly ACCEPT or REJECT.","network.jinn.binary-judgment.item-sha256":"sha256:a0b1f6d782605c507e665ef761601fe6bccfa265d1750165f62bfe4aa42a9178","outputs":[{"mediaType":"text/plain; charset=utf-8","name":"judge-response","required":true},{"mediaType":"application/vnd.jinn.binary-judgment.observation.v1+json","name":"judge-observation","required":true},{"mediaType":"application/vnd.inspect-ai.eval-log+json","name":"inspect-log","required":false}],"payload":{"candidateAnswer":"Calvin and Dave have nostalgic memories about their dads.","evidence":"[D12:2 | 1:12 pm on 3 August, 2023] Dave: Hey Calvin, I understand the stress of getting a car serviced. Fixing cars is like therapy for me. Growing up working on cars with my dad, refurbishing them gives me a sense of fulfillment.\n[D20:6 | 8:57 pm on 22 September, 2023] Calvin: Yeah, there's this one song that always makes me smile. It played during a road trip with my dad and we had so much fun singing along to it.","itemId":"urn:uuid:4b8dc429-8fa7-55a1-8e74-002e09e915eb","provenance":{"sourceCommitment":"sha256:846ba50e2b05c0c1c8bb062b8a78d422fd5b54fe10a8f3e1c752d594685e9a1d","timestamp":"2026-04-02T14:22:55Z"},"question":"Which of their family member do Calvin and Dave have nostalgic memories about?","referenceAnswer":"Dad","sources":[{"digest":{"sha256":"846ba50e2b05c0c1c8bb062b8a78d422fd5b54fe10a8f3e1c752d594685e9a1d"}}]},"profile":{"digest":{"sha256":"ebb34d8362e2cc3135847a5ad6f3ee3d9c2d9922a2b827aa9dfcbaf440b22557"},"uri":"https://spec.jinn.network/task-profiles/binary-judgment/2.0"},"protocol":"https://spec.jinn.network/profiles/task-execution/v1"}